            <div xml:id="d904">

                <pb facs="1411" n="1397" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1397"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 EW/11–2744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-07T14:00:00-04:00">December 7, 1944—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2798. Your 4524, November 27, 5 p.m. Question of extending terms of reference of
                    War Crimes Commission to include German war crimes in Italy, was raised by
                    British with this Government last spring. We concurred in their proposal, and in
                    suggestion that it be discussed by Advisory Council for Italy but we have not
                    ourselves taken any other action.</p>
                <p>Pell, American representative on War Crimes Commission, London, is being
                    instructed to forward minutes of meetings and other pertinent documents direct
                    to Moscow if copies are available.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
